@startuml
!include style-usecase.iuml
left to right direction
title Planit Stage 2 — implemented use cases through GUI or CLI
actor "Local organizer / planner" as Planner
rectangle "Planit — JavaFX dashboard OR CLI (shared controller/facade)" {
  usecase "Manage event, constraints,\nteam and availability" as Setup
  usecase "F01: Add ideas and fuse\ninto concepts" as F01
  usecase "F02: Generate, inspect, select\nand approve blueprint" as F02
  usecase "F03: Generate/revise tasks,\ncheck deadlines, approve/discard" as F03
  usecase "F04: Build/revise agenda,\ncheck conflicts, approve/discard" as F04
  usecase "F05: Budget/catering proposal,\nedit allocations, validate/approve" as F05
  usecase "F06: Research/manual venues\nand compare evidence" as F06
  usecase "F07: Simulate what-if\nwithout changing real plan" as F07
  usecase "F08: Propose/confirm/discard\nreal changes; generate contingency" as F08
  usecase "F09a: Generate/edit/approve\ncommunication drafts" as F09a
  usecase "F09b: Ask saved-fact FAQ\nor receive unknown response" as F09b
  usecase "F10: Record actual outcomes\nand generate analysis" as F10
  usecase "Reopen saved plans /\nsequential GUI–CLI handoff" as Load
}
Planner -- Setup
Planner -- F01
Planner -- F02
Planner -- F03
Planner -- F04
Planner -- F05
Planner -- F06
Planner -- F07
Planner -- F08
Planner -- F09a
Planner -- F09b
Planner -- F10
Planner -- Load
note right of F06
  Supporting services across these use cases:
  Gemini: F01–F10 generation/analysis except local FAQ.
  Places: F05 provider discovery, F06 research.
  Edits, approvals, actuals recording and FAQ are local.
  Provider participation is not every action in a label.
  See class-04 and SD03/SD08 for API relationships.
end note
note bottom of Planner
  No login, roles or separate attendee portal.
  Organizer can enter member ideas and ask attendee questions.
  Both interfaces expose F01–F10; no concurrent shared-store sessions.
end note
note bottom of Load
  Successful meaningful mutations autosave.
  Read-only FAQ and simulations do not save new facts.
  F03/F04 require approval if blueprint alternatives exist.
  No weather, booking or send/publish integration.
end note
legend bottom
  Solid actor associations denote participation, not call order.
  No <<include>>/<<extend>> asserted for optional provider use or workflow order.
  External service participation is summarized in the note to avoid crossing actor lines.
endlegend
@enduml
